# Vanilla target (HTML / JS / CSS)

There is **no separate `packages/vanilla`** — plain HTML/JS/CSS is served by `@rosettadash/web-components` plus documented snippets. This rule defines that consumer contract.

## Mental model

| Need | Use |
|------|-----|
| Single component, no bundler | CE tag + `registerRd*()` + optional `tokens.css` |
| Media pipeline (video, wasm) | `@rosettadash/web-components/browser/media` ESM bundle |
| Theming | `tokens.css` and/or `styles.css` imports |

Framework packages are optional sugar — vanilla consumers must reach parity via WC alone.

## Minimal snippet shape

Every README/snippet must include:

1. **CSS imports** (optional but documented)
2. **Module script** that registers the CE
3. **HTML** using the `rd-*` tag
4. **Event listening** via `addEventListener` on the element

```html
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/node_modules/@rosettadash/web-components/tokens.css" />

<rd-chart-bar title="Sales"></rd-chart-bar>

<script type="module">
  import { registerRdBarChart } from '@rosettadash/web-components/visual/chart/bar';
  registerRdBarChart();
</script>
```

## Configuration without JS frameworks

- Prefer **attributes** for scalars (`title`, `label`, `accept`)
- Use **`element.setProperty('markers', array)`** for objects (document in snippet comments)
- Use **`data-*`** only for progressive enhancement hooks — not as primary API

## Styling

- Host page sets `--rd-*` on `:root` or a wrapper — components inherit
- Do not require Tailwind/Bootstrap in snippets
- Document minimal vs themed modes (`12-styling-tokens-and-css.mdc`)

## Media / no-build apps

```html
<script type="module" src="/node_modules/@rosettadash/web-components/browser/media.js"></script>
```

Document COOP/COEP and same-origin `@ffmpeg/core` when wasm is involved (`30-media-and-video.mdc`).

## Snippet maintenance

When changing a manual CE's attributes or events:

- [ ] Update WC README section
- [ ] Update Storybook catalog row (shared mount)
- [ ] Verify snippet works without a bundler (import maps or esm.sh noted if helpful)

## Future `packages/vanilla`

If promoted later: move snippets to `packages/vanilla/examples/` and keep WC as implementation — this rule's API contract unchanged.

